+## 7. ET re-parameterization (R3 mesh implementation, 2026-10-05)
+
+The approved mesh ET implementation uses one atmospheric demand volume per
+cell. Actual surface evaporation spends it first; soil ET spends only the
+remaining accumulated past demand. Stress is evaluated once at the extraction
+site (SIGMA top layer, CLOSED_FORM bulk, ENSLAVED equilibrium surface).
+`WILTING_SUCTION` is a positive project length or Automatic 150 m. There is no
+infiltration-positive gate; capillary rise is an internal transfer. Kernel
+cells use these controls instead of lumped `UEF` / `LED`; ordinary lumped
+`[GROUNDWATER]` keeps those legacy controls.
+
+Automatic mesh ET resolves `BOTH`; explicit `NONE` is retained. New automatic
+link exchange uses `LINK_SEEPAGE DEFAULT`, resolving `TWO_WAY`; explicit old
+`AUTO` remains one-way and saves as `ONE_WAY`. See the required
+[migration guidance and evidence](SURFACE_PROCESS_R3_IMPLEMENTATION_2026-10-05.md).
+`M_LAYERS` remains the number of sigma soil layers; `LTS_TIERS` controls time
+cadences, and changing one does not change the other. Sigma advection remains
+first-order upwind. Shared demand for subcatchment/LID footprints and snow
+coverage still needs the R4/R5/UEB area interfaces; mesh budget qualification
+does not certify those paths.
 
